# Cloudflare Pages internal rewrites only.
# Never redirect .html destinations back to their source paths: those reverse
# rules can re-enter these rewrites. Pages handles native HTML normalization.
# Do not add trailing-slash redirects here.
# Pretty share links -> the shared-post landing page.
#
# These are 200 rewrites: the edge serves shared-post.html's bytes while the
# browser URL stays /post/<id>. Putting ?post=:id on the destination does NOT
# forward a query string to the client -- it only steers the edge's internal
# file lookup -- so app.js reads the post id from location.pathname and treats
# ?post= / ?post_id= / ?id= as a fallback. Do not "restore" the query here.
/post/:id          /shared-post.html          200
/p/:id             /shared-post.html          200
# Clean page routes; keep these ahead of the catch-all.
/about             /about.html              200
/download          /download.html           200
/contact           /contact.html            200
/credits           /credits.html            200
/shared-post       /shared-post.html        200
/privacy           /privacy.html            200
# SPA-style fallback for anything else (real files always win over this rule).
/*                 /index.html                  200
